   <widget class="QLabel" name="label5">
    <property name="geometry">
     <rect>
      <x>15</x>
      <y>20</y>
      <width>468</width>
      <height>214</height>
     </rect>
    </property>
    <property name="text">
     <string>If a LCD display is connected to a feedback decoder, the decoder can display the speed of the train currently driving through a dedicated track. Two tracks can be monitored per feedback decoder. If such track gets occupied, the decoder starts a timer, which is stopped as soon as one of the adjacent tracks gets occupied. Since the length of the track is known, the speed can be calculated. The speed is expressed in Km/h (and thus compensated for the fact that trains are in H0 scale).</string>
    </property>
    <property name="alignment">
     <set>Qt::AlignLeft|Qt::AlignTop</set>
    </property>
    <property name="wordWrap">
     <bool>true</bool>
    </property>
   </widget>
  </widget>
